questions.prompt:
This Express server works on one machine but breaks when you run 4 copies behind a load balancer. Find the bug and fix it.

```js
const loginAttempts = {}; // ip -> count

app.post('/login', (req, res) => {
  loginAttempts[req.ip] = (loginAttempts[req.ip] ?? 0) + 1;
  if (loginAttempts[req.ip] > 5) return res.status(429).send('Too many attempts');
  // ... check password ...
});
```

questions.answer:
Each process has its own `loginAttempts`, so the limit is per server (≈20 tries across 4 servers) and resets on restart. Move it to a shared store:
```js
app.post('/login', async (req, res) => {
  const key = `login:${req.ip}`;
  const count = await redis.incr(key);        // atomic across all servers
  if (count === 1) await redis.expire(key, 900); // reset after 15 minutes
  if (count > 5) return res.status(429).send('Too many attempts');
  // ... check password ...
});
```
